{"name":"Longing for Nature","hex":"#4b9f5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"longing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of long"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["This term needs a definition. Please help out and add a definition, then remove the text {{rfdef}}."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/longing"},{"term":"for","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Fore."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["Because."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for"},{"term":"nature","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The way things are, the totality of all things in the physical universe and their order, especially the physical world in contrast to spiritual realms and flora and fauna as distinct from human conventions, art, and technology.","The particular way someone or something is, especially\nThe essential or innate characteristics of a person or thing which will always tend to manifest, especially in contrast to specific contexts, reason, religious duty, upbringing, and personal pretense or effort."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To endow with natural qualities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nature"}],"entries":[{"title":"Longing (Bell Witch album)","blocks":[{"text":"Longing is the debut studio album by the Seattle-based doom metal band Bell Witch, released on November 13, 2012 through Profound Lore Records. The album began Bell Witch's trend of slow, low, and mournful music for which the band would become known."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6c/Longing_%282012%29_cover.jpg/330px-Longing_%282012%29_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longing_(Bell_Witch_album)","wikidata":"Q55621222"},{"title":"Longing For","blocks":[{"text":"Longing For is the sixth studio album by Taiwanese recording artist Rainie Yang. It was released on July 29, 2011, by Sony Music Taiwan with two covers: a Blue Sky Edition and Starry Night Edition."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Longing_for....jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longing_For","wikidata":"Q4352081"},{"title":"Nature","blocks":[{"text":"Nature, in the broadest sense, is the physical world or universe. In this general sense nature refers to the laws, elements and phenomena of the physical world, including life. Although humans are part of nature, human activity or humans as a whole are often described as at times at odds, or outright separate and even superior to nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Startrails_above_Gunung_Bromo_-_Indonesia.jpg/330px-Startrails_above_Gunung_Bromo_-_Indonesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature","wikidata":"Q7860"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg/500px-The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg/1280px-The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg/500px-The_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Blue Marble, which is a famous view of the Earth, taken in 1972 by the crew of Apollo 17","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Blue_Marble%2C_AS17-148-22727.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Tectonic_plate_boundaries.png/500px-Tecto